From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 04:08:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Refuse forwarded logins without a BungeeGuard token
 (pandaspigot.yml bungeeGuardTokens)

With bungeecord on, whoever reaches the server's port can claim any UUID; the only defence was that
nobody but the proxy could reach it. Velocity's BUNGEEGUARD forwarding adds a bungeeguard-token
profile property holding its forwarding secret. When bungeeGuardTokens lists tokens, a login must
carry exactly one property whose value is one of them, compared in constant time, or it is refused
and the real remote address is logged. The token is removed from the profile, which otherwise goes to
every player in the tab list. No tokens configured: unchanged behaviour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

